-- Native role routing (s54), ASCII twin: a spawn `at` a kanji point binding routes into the kanji 位置 column, mints an id into the kanji 鍵 column, and fills the kanji 親 column with the carrier row — all three declared by `role`, not by the literal names pos/keys/parent — so the fully native world spawns positioned, keyed, parented rows.
-- The spawn machinery finds its columns by declared role, never by magic English names: a world with no column called pos still places its children.
--! registry ../registries/s54-native-roles.reg
--! expect-n 3
--! expect 手先 = 0 0 1
--! expect 位置 = 5 5 6 6 7 8
--! expect 資金 = 100 200 25
--! expect 鍵 = 10 20 21
--! expect 親 = -1 -1 1

生成器 , spawn 手先 at 出現
